      "problem": "Which of the following is equivalent to $2x≡1\\,(\\text{mod}\\,15)?$",
      "worked_solution": "The scalar multiplication properties of congruences state that for $k\\in Z,$ we have the following:\n\n- $a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟹\\,ka≡kb\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)$\n\n- $a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟹\\,ka≡kb\\,(\\text{mod}\\,kn)$\n\nThe modulus equals $15$ in all statements, which suggests we'll need to use the first property.\n\nNotice that the coefficient of $x$ is $2,$ and $8\\cdot 2=16$ is one larger than the modulus. Therefore, we can reduce the coefficient of $x$ to unity as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & ≡1\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,15) \\\\ 8\\cdot 2x & ≡8\\cdot 1\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,15) \\\\ 16x & ≡8\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,15) \\\\ x+15x & ≡8\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,15) \\\\ x+0x & ≡8\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,15) \\\\ x & ≡8\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,15)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
